#> Demonstrates the 3-bit Incrementer: hold, count up, and overflow wraparound.
vcd trace.vcd

#> `counter` starts at 0, thanks to `initial it <= 0`.
assert counter == 0

#> With `increment` low, the counter holds its value.
poke increment false
tick 2
assert counter == 0

#> Raise `increment`: the counter counts up on every cycle.
poke increment true
tick 1
assert counter == 1
tick 3
assert counter == 4

#> Three more ticks reach the top of the 3-bit range...
tick 3
assert counter == 7

#> ...and the next tick overflows, wrapping back to 0.
tick 1
assert counter == 0
tick 2
assert counter == 2

show
exit
